    "summary": "A high school debate coach asks the assistant to help \"steelman\" (build the strongest possible version of) arguments for strict border security and increased enforcement. The assistant provides several philosophical justifications for the affirmative side, including the \"just-offense\" argument, and then undergoes a significant breakdown in coherence when asked how to counter humanitarian criticisms.",
